       MATCH: all 58 mapped state elements identical every cycle

Interpretation:
  ARM C removes every X from the netlist yet still diverges from RTL.
  X-freedom is therefore NOT evidence that gate activity is valid.
  ARM E shares ONE power-up vector across both models -> lockstep.
  Constrained ARM E fixes rf[1] (state boot firmware guarantees) and
  sweeps the remaining 44 free elements: every member stays in lockstep
  AND runs the full workload, so its activity is valid for power.

